CloudBurrow patch 97 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1814). Applies after patch 0095.

A positional parameter alone in the select list had no type: positional
parameters were left undeclared, and an undeclared parameter with no type
from its context is an INT64, so `SELECT ? AS a` with a STRING failed
("strconv.ParseInt ... invalid syntax") and a FLOAT64 or BOOL was truncated
to an integer. BigQuery gives the column the parameter's type
(https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/parameterized-queries). A
statement's positional parameters are now declared, in order, when it has
no more `?` than args and every arg is a scalar of a known type; undeclared
parameters are turned off for that statement (go-googlesql allows no
declared positional parameter while they are allowed) and back on after
it. An ARRAY, STRUCT or NULL arg leaves them undeclared, as before.

A Go value cannot be a NUMERIC, BIGNUMERIC, DATE, TIME, DATETIME,
GEOGRAPHY, JSON or INTERVAL, so a named parameter of those types (as the
emulator binds them, from text) was a STRING, and a DATETIME a TIMESTAMP.
TypedParameter{Type, Value} binds the value of the type it names from its
REST text (BYTES base64-encoded), and a parameter bound as one has that
type.

bare_positional_parameter_test.go (TestBarePositionalParameter).

